   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "It has been accepted that life on the Earth started out as single celled, simple organisms, which then evolved into complex organisms. How did evolution proceed to produce such a wide variety of living organisms from a simple ancestor?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 720124,
     "content_html": "Prokaryotes produced the fungi, then the protists which then branches to plants and animals."
